    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I need to prep a quick brief for our CTO about our scaling strategy. Can you give me a high-level summary of the differences between vertical scaling and horizontal scaling? I need to explain it to someone who understands the business side but isn't a devops expert, so keep it professional but clear.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Vertical scaling means increasing the power of a single existing server, like giving one machine more RAM or CPU. Think of it as making one employee much stronger. Horizontal scaling involves adding more smaller servers to share the workload, like hiring more employees to handle the volume. The choice depends on whether you want to boost one machine or spread the load across many.",
