    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. one more thing though—when we're dealing with these sudden, unpredictable spikes in traffic, what are the actual risks of not having automated scaling set up? like, if we're just relying on manual intervention, what kind of issues usually pop up in the system?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Relying on manual scaling during unexpected traffic spikes leads directly to service degradation or outright outages, as human response time is too slow for rapid load changes. The immediate risk is increased latency, meaning users experience slow application performance, leading to poor customer experience and abandoned transactions. Without automation, you risk crashing your infrastructure entirely under sudden load, resulting in lost revenue and reputational damage.",
      "source": "target",
